  "body": "Approved public YouTube channels can now feed the canonical recording catalog through bounded, resumable executions. Provider outages retain checkpoints and availability, concurrent requests share a source lock, and full reconciliation directly rechecks known resources after traversing uploads. The admin page exposes approvals, stop controls, dry runs, and continuation of saved executions.\n\nVerified thumbnail metadata stays tied to the video identity, editorial overrides survive refreshes, and non-embeddable videos use provider links. Nonpublic or expired provider data is cleared with audited identity retained. The migration enables no sources and starts the worker disabled; exact migration provenance and real PostgreSQL/Haskell probes are included in CI.\n\nValidation: 3,539 Hspec examples passed (six pending), 15 focused UI tests, UI typecheck and focused lint, 10 browser regressions across Chromium desktop/phone/tablet, Firefox and WebKit, database rollback/reapplication and concurrency probes, 82 release-tooling tests, repository checks and existing formal-methods audit. Full Stack executable build passed after local disk exhaustion was resolved. Production schema verification and reviewed inventories were updated to match the additive migration.\n\nRollout: see docs/records-ingestion/runtime-rollout.md. This extends the previously merged thumbnail correction; it does not authorize event publication. Event coverage and shared pilot controls remain separate work, and optional event ends are covered by #460. Staging/production deployment remains blocked by the previously observed Fly overdue-invoice HTTP 403; no production backfill or scheduled execution is claimed. Required independent review and guarded release checks remain mandatory.\n",
